    <!-- Sonic Upscaling Enhancer (SUE) — Lossy Engine -->
    <string name="settings_sue_title">Lossy Audio Restoration</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_disabled_description">Disabled — enable to reconstruct harmonics and spatiality lost during lossy compression.</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_enabled_lossy_description">Active — reconstructing harmonics and spatiality for compressed audio.</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_enabled_lossless_description">Enabled, but inactive — lossless files are played without lossy enhancement.</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_enabled_idle_description">Reconstructs harmonics and spatiality lost during lossy compression.</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_enabled_bypass_description">Enabled, but currently bypassed — this source does not need enhancement.</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_unavailable_description">Enabled, but unavailable — this build could not initialize the native SUE pipeline.</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_status_codec">Source codec: %1$s</string>
    <string name="settings_sue_status_profile">Profile: %1$s</string>
    <string name="dialog_lossy_restorer_title">How it works: Lossy Restorer</string>
    <string name="dialog_lossy_restorer_body">Lossy compression (MP3, AAC, Opus…) permanently deletes high-frequency detail and can narrow the stereo image to save space. This engine does not use "AI magic" — it is purely mathematical DSP that scales its intensity to how much damage the source codec and bitrate actually did:\n\n• Synthesizes the missing high-frequency harmonics.\n• Widens the stereo field on the most heavily compressed sources, where it has collapsed the most.\n• Smooths intermodulation artifacts with a gentle low-pass, then closes with a true-peak limiter so every added stage stays clipping-free.\n\nClean, high-bitrate lossy files may need little or no processing and are automatically bypassed — as are lossless files, to preserve bit-perfect playback.</string>

    <!-- Hi-Res Dynamic Remaster — Lossless Engine -->
    <string name="settings_hires_remaster_title">Hi-Res Dynamic Remaster</string>
    <string name="settings_hires_remaster_enabled_description">Gently expands dynamics and oversamples lossless sources up to 96kHz; already-hi-res tracks are left untouched.</string>
    <string name="settings_hires_remaster_disabled_description">Hi-Res Dynamic Remaster is disabled.</string>
    <string name="dialog_hires_remaster_title">How it works: Hi-Res Remaster</string>
    <string name="dialog_hires_remaster_body">Modern music is often over-compressed in the studio to sound louder (the Loudness War), sacrificing dynamic punch. This engine works only on lossless sources (FLAC, ALAC, WAV…) that aren\'t already native hi-res — those are left completely untouched. On eligible tracks it acts as a mastering chain:\n\n• Applies a gentle upward expansion to transients — never compression — so drum hits and peaks regain up to ~2.5dB of the punch flattened by loudness-war mastering, while quiet passages stay untouched.\n• Oversamples the source (44.1→88.2kHz or 48→96kHz) so the expansion and limiting stages have clean headroom to work in.\n• Closes with a true-peak limiter so the added dynamics and the oversampling never clip, with the initial gain automatically tucked in based on the track\'s own peak level.\n\nLossy files are unaffected by this engine — they go through the Restorer instead.</string>
